  "description": "Erection of piggy back roof extension to a first floor flat with rear juliet balcony, installation of 4 nos side rooflights. Raising ridge height.",
  "development_type": "Other house holder developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "Prior to the commencement of any development above ground level, samples of the facing materials to be utilised in the development to which this permission relates shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved samples.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The works shall be carried out and maintained in accordance with the deposited Fire Statement compliant with Policy D12(A).\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan 2021\r",
    "Prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates, the requirements and enhancements as set out on page 7 of Bat Emergence and Re Entry  Survey report prepared by Arbtech Consulting Ltd dated 18 June 2026 shall be implemented in full and permanently retained thereafter. The applicant shall install at least one integrated  bat box within the new roof extension of the building (to be installed away from windows and artificial light sources) on a southerly aspect. In respect of external lighting within the development, this must be kept to a minimum and follow the guidance from the Guidance Note GN08/23 Bats and Artificial Lighting Bat Night - Bat Conservation Trust and Institution of Lighting Professionals)  (2023). \r\rReason: To safeguard the biodiversity and nature conservation value of the site, in accordance with policy G6 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS3 and DM6 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r"
  ],
